1
00:00:08,049 --> 00:00:12,387
KIAN'S B&B KARAOKE

2
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:15,015
- He needs to turn off the song now.
- I know.

3
00:00:15,098 --> 00:00:16,516
- He has to turn it off.
- It's time.

4
00:00:17,642 --> 00:00:20,228
LOOK OVER HERE

5
00:00:20,854 --> 00:00:21,980
- Turn it off.
- Hey.

6
00:00:22,063 --> 00:00:23,064
FRANTICALLY

7
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:24,482
- He has to turn it off.
- Right.

8
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:25,442
He's turning it off.

9
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:26,735
HE TURNS IT OFF IN TIME

10
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:29,320
- Great job!
- One more song!

11
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:31,823
- Are you ready? Do you have the ring?
- Yes.

12
00:00:31,906 --> 00:00:33,742
Let's go to bed now.

13
00:00:33,825 --> 00:00:34,909
All of a sudden?

14
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:37,245
So, the thing is,

15
00:00:37,328 --> 00:00:42,125
this person used to be
a professional athlete.

16
00:00:42,208 --> 00:00:44,461
- What?
- And they're working hard at Kian's B&B.

17
00:00:44,544 --> 00:00:45,837
What's he talking about?

18
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:49,007
It's our employee Kim Yeon-koung,

19
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:50,383
and today is her birthday.

20
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:51,301
Don't.

21
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:53,803
- For real?
- No way.

22
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:55,013
- Seriously?
- Oh, my gosh.

23
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:56,848
So this is why you pushed it to midnight?

24
00:00:58,516 --> 00:01:00,435
It is midnight! On the dot!

25
00:01:00,518 --> 00:01:02,395
So he pushed it to midnight on purpose.

26
00:01:02,479 --> 00:01:04,397
LIGHTING THE CANDLES IN THE BACK

27
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:06,191
STANDING BY

28
00:01:06,274 --> 00:01:08,651
She's probably feeling shy right now.

29
00:01:08,735 --> 00:01:10,695
- Don't we have to sing the song?
- Right.

30
00:01:10,779 --> 00:01:12,822
The birthday song.

31
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:16,284
The song.

32
00:01:16,367 --> 00:01:17,786
THEY START SIGNALING AGAIN

33
00:01:17,869 --> 00:01:19,412
LOOK AT US

34
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:20,872
The song.

35
00:01:20,955 --> 00:01:23,124
Sing the song.

36
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:24,834
The birthday song.

37
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:26,961
Let's sing the birthday song!

38
00:01:27,045 --> 00:01:28,088
GETS THE MESSAGE

39
00:01:28,963 --> 00:01:29,798
Go!

40
00:01:29,881 --> 00:01:31,591
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

41
00:01:31,674 --> 00:01:34,969
<i>- Happy birthday to you</i>
<i>- Happy birthday to you</i>

42
00:01:35,053 --> 00:01:38,056
<i>- Happy birthday to you</i>
<i>- Happy birthday to you</i>

43
00:01:38,139 --> 00:01:38,973
What on earth?

44
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:41,100
You're so tall!

45
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:42,644
Dear Kim Yeon-koung!

46
00:01:42,727 --> 00:01:43,728
Put it on right for me.

47
00:01:43,812 --> 00:01:47,190
<i>- Happy birthday to you</i>
<i>- Happy birthday to you</i>

48
00:01:47,774 --> 00:01:48,983
- What's this?
- Put it on.

49
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:50,777
- I have to wear it?
- Put it on her.

50
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:53,780
- It's a <i>kimjang</i> vest.
- I'm feeling embarrassed.

51
00:01:54,405 --> 00:01:57,200
Come on, you should've given me
something expensive then.

52
00:01:58,618 --> 00:01:59,911
Let me put it on for you.

53
00:01:59,994 --> 00:02:01,246
Do you even know my size?

54
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:02,664
Thank you.

55
00:02:03,456 --> 00:02:04,833
- The goddess!
- It's perfect on you!

56
00:02:04,916 --> 00:02:06,626
- She's a goddess!
- She's a goddess!

57
00:02:08,586 --> 00:02:10,630
Can we sing the birthday song
in the Indian way?

58
00:02:10,713 --> 00:02:12,006
What will you do?

59
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:13,133
Please do it for us.

60
00:02:16,511 --> 00:02:18,930
CELEBRATING HER BIRTHDAY
THE INDIAN WAY AS WELL

61
00:02:19,013 --> 00:02:21,641
Do it while dancing.

62
00:02:25,645 --> 00:02:26,688
CLOSING EYES

63
00:02:35,029 --> 00:02:36,156
Thank you.

64
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:38,324
Okay, hold this for a moment.

65
00:02:38,408 --> 00:02:39,826
I was wondering where you went.

66
00:02:39,909 --> 00:02:42,370
- Come on.
- Seriously.

67
00:02:42,453 --> 00:02:44,122
We planned to do it at midnight,

68
00:02:44,205 --> 00:02:46,457
but you wanted to go to bed
at 11:00 p.m. so badly.

69
00:02:46,541 --> 00:02:48,835
- Right.
- So we were torn.

70
00:02:48,918 --> 00:02:51,129
You felt particularly tired today.

71
00:02:51,212 --> 00:02:53,047
- And you wanted to go to bed early.
- Yeah.

72
00:02:53,131 --> 00:02:54,674
After I took a shower…

73
00:02:54,757 --> 00:02:56,926
- Yeah, didn't you become sleepy?
- Yeah, totally.

74
00:02:57,010 --> 00:03:01,055
So since it's your birthday,
just rest until lunchtime tomorrow.

75
00:03:01,139 --> 00:03:02,891
- Really?
- It's your birthday present.

76
00:03:03,975 --> 00:03:04,809
Yeah.

77
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:07,228
Rest until lunchtime.

78
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:09,188
Then, can I go home tonight?

79
00:03:09,272 --> 00:03:11,649
That might be a bit tough.
Just rest until lunchtime.

80
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:12,817
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

81
00:03:12,901 --> 00:03:15,194
What am I going to do here
until then though?

82
00:03:16,362 --> 00:03:18,907
Feel free to wash up or keep hanging out.

83
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:20,116
- Yeah? Okay.
- Okay.

84
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:24,162
When the TV was opening up,
Kian was in the back and about to cry.

85
00:03:24,245 --> 00:03:25,330
Really?

86
00:03:27,123 --> 00:03:29,500
THE BOSS WAS MOVED
BY THE KARAOKE ROOM OPENING

87
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:31,544
He was like,
"Finally, I get to show this."

88
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:33,755
That part was built last.

89
00:03:33,838 --> 00:03:34,923
At first,

90
00:03:35,548 --> 00:03:39,427
I thought of just letting people
use it freely, like a coin karaoke room,

91
00:03:39,510 --> 00:03:41,304
and opening it on some days.

92
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:43,348
But now that we're here,

93
00:03:43,431 --> 00:03:45,850
it turned into like a concert stage.

94
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:48,603
Yeah, when I got up there,
it did feel like a stage.

95
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:50,146
- It did?
- Yeah.

96
00:03:52,190 --> 00:03:53,483
It did feel like a stage.

97
00:03:54,275 --> 00:03:56,277
We should go to bed soon.

98
00:03:56,903 --> 00:03:58,571
Lights-out in ten minutes.

99
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:02,116
- Good night.
- Have a good night.

100
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,618
- Happy birthday.
- Thank you.

101
00:04:03,701 --> 00:04:06,079
- You too, even though it was yesterday.
- Just a day apart.

102
00:04:06,162 --> 00:04:07,121
Good night.

103
00:04:07,789 --> 00:04:08,915
Good night, everyone.

104
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:11,125
Thank you, Jun-ho.

105
00:04:11,209 --> 00:04:12,460
Have a good night.

106
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:13,503
- Good night.
- You too.

107
00:04:13,586 --> 00:04:14,879
You're sleeping there, right?

108
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:16,422
- Yes.
- I'm sleeping there too.

109
00:04:18,091 --> 00:04:19,092
Nice!

110
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:21,469
Good night.

111
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:23,471
My goodness! Good night.

112
00:04:23,554 --> 00:04:26,057
- It's the last night for you two.
- Yes.

113
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,267
- It is.
- The last night.

114
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:28,559
Yes, thank you for everything.

115
00:04:28,643 --> 00:04:30,395
- Did you have fun?
- Yes, so much.

116
00:04:30,478 --> 00:04:31,771
- Really?
- Yes.

117
00:04:31,854 --> 00:04:34,440
- Have a good night.
- Bye. Good night.

118
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:38,444
BOSS GOES TO BED TOO

119
00:04:39,028 --> 00:04:40,989
- Good night.
- Good night.

120
00:04:41,948 --> 00:04:44,158
- I don't want to leave tomorrow.
- Me neither.

121
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:46,119
THE 4 FRESHMEN CAN'T SLEEP AND GET UP

122
00:04:46,202 --> 00:04:47,578
We go home and it's over tomorrow.

123
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:49,330
- We'll come visit Gwangju.
- Sure.

124
00:04:49,414 --> 00:04:50,540
I think I'll go to Seoul.

125
00:04:50,623 --> 00:04:52,875
- Call me if you do.
- I will.

126
00:04:52,959 --> 00:04:54,836
I'll give you a nice tour of Seoul.

127
00:04:54,919 --> 00:04:56,087
Okay, thanks.

128
00:04:56,921 --> 00:04:58,631
Can we follow each other on IG?

129
00:04:58,715 --> 00:04:59,882
Let's do it.

130
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:01,509
- Let's all follow each other.
- Yeah.

131
00:05:02,135 --> 00:05:04,637
When you first came,
you were having so much fun.

132
00:05:04,721 --> 00:05:06,556
- It was hard to approach you.
- Sorry.

133
00:05:07,181 --> 00:05:08,182
Really energetic, right?

134
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:09,726
Yeah, totally.

135
00:05:09,809 --> 00:05:10,977
Darn it.

136
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:13,980
I wanted to appear like
a nonchalant city girl.

137
00:05:21,654 --> 00:05:24,741
DAY 3

138
00:05:25,408 --> 00:05:28,286
7:30 A.M.
JUN-HO GETS UP

139
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:38,296
YEON-KOUNG GETS UP

140
00:05:38,379 --> 00:05:41,340
SHE STRETCHES AS SOON AS SHE GETS UP

141
00:05:45,428 --> 00:05:48,931
ZUHA GETS UP TOO

142
00:05:53,561 --> 00:05:55,313
- Did you sleep well?
- Yes.

143
00:05:59,609 --> 00:06:03,404
SHE FINDS OUT HOW TO GET OUT EASILY
ON THE 3RD DAY

144
00:06:09,243 --> 00:06:11,579
WHILE THE EMPLOYEES ARE UP EARLY

145
00:06:11,662 --> 00:06:13,372
THE BOSS IS STILL SOUND ASLEEP

146
00:06:15,583 --> 00:06:17,585
KIAN'S B&B

147
00:06:24,842 --> 00:06:28,346
THE PRIEST GOES SOMEWHERE

148
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:33,893
HE OPENS A BOOK?

149
00:06:33,976 --> 00:06:35,728
O Lord, save me.

150
00:06:35,812 --> 00:06:37,980
Lord, come quickly and help me.

151
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:39,774
Glory to the Father, Son, and Holy Spirit.

152
00:06:39,857 --> 00:06:42,318
As it was in the beginning,
is now, and ever shall be. Amen.

153
00:06:42,401 --> 00:06:43,402
Your words, Lord…

154
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:46,697
<i>Catholic clerics</i>
<i>are obligated to pray daily,</i>

155
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:48,991
<i>but I had to be considerate</i>
<i>of others' faiths.</i>

156
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:51,536
<i>So I went outside to do my duty.</i>

157
00:06:52,954 --> 00:06:54,038
Let us pray.

158
00:06:57,166 --> 00:07:01,587
THE BOSS IS UP

159
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:22,692
HE FINISHES A 3-MINUTE SHOWER

160
00:07:26,362 --> 00:07:29,240
FIRST CHANGE OF UNDERWEAR ON THE 3RD DAY

161
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:31,534
- Did you sleep well?
- Yes.

162
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:35,371
- You're sad, aren't you?
- Yes.

163
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:36,706
I don't want to go home.

164
00:07:36,789 --> 00:07:38,541
SAD

165
00:07:38,624 --> 00:07:40,376
I really want to stay.

166
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,003
- Where are you going?
- Well…

167
00:07:42,086 --> 00:07:43,337
Back to your part-time job?

168
00:07:43,421 --> 00:07:45,756
- Just until this Sunday.
- When does school start?

169
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:47,508
On March 3. Next Tuesday.

170
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:49,093
Next week… It's next week?

171
00:07:49,177 --> 00:07:50,136
Yes.

172
00:07:50,219 --> 00:07:52,638
After the entrance ceremony,
there's an orientation.

173
00:07:52,722 --> 00:07:55,558
Your orientation will feel
similar to this.

174
00:07:55,641 --> 00:07:57,143
- Really?
- Similar to this?

175
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:58,269
Yeah, it'll be like this.

176
00:07:58,895 --> 00:08:00,313
I've only been here for a day,

177
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:02,440
and I already feel comfortable.

178
00:08:02,523 --> 00:08:04,942
You got along well
as soon as you got here.

179
00:08:05,026 --> 00:08:06,944
I'm used to being in groups.

180
00:08:07,028 --> 00:08:09,197
- Right, living in dorms.
- I think it helps.

181
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,531
We always say

182
00:08:10,615 --> 00:08:12,617
priests must know how to be on their own

183
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:15,620
and also know
how to get along in a community.

184
00:08:15,703 --> 00:08:20,875
I think that's a virtue
everyone should have.

185
00:08:20,958 --> 00:08:21,834
Right.

186
00:08:22,835 --> 00:08:24,378
You must be ready now. Come sit.

187
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:25,838
I'm pretty much ready.

188
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:28,883
You know, we're all friends
who were born in 1989.

189
00:08:28,966 --> 00:08:30,259
- You're right.
- Right.

190
00:08:30,343 --> 00:08:32,345
But I'm still the youngest at my temple.

191
00:08:32,428 --> 00:08:33,804
I need juniors.

192
00:08:33,888 --> 00:08:35,389
I was scolded yesterday too.

193
00:08:35,473 --> 00:08:37,350
Always the youngest
and always getting scolded.

194
00:08:37,892 --> 00:08:39,477
But the bright side is

195
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:42,021
when I'm scolded
and corrected by my elders,

196
00:08:42,104 --> 00:08:45,191
I don't become arrogant
or think I'm always right.

197
00:08:47,276 --> 00:08:48,653
Are you leaving tomorrow?

198
00:08:48,736 --> 00:08:49,820
Yes.

199
00:08:49,904 --> 00:08:51,197
Tonight's the last night.

200
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:53,032
- We should use the jacuzzi tonight.
- Right.

201
00:08:53,115 --> 00:08:55,576
Jacuzzi? We still haven't used it yet.

202
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:57,495
- You still haven't?
- Never.

203
00:08:57,578 --> 00:08:58,829
I think we should.

204
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:00,831
I need to try the trampoline too.

205
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:02,083
Try it now.

206
00:09:03,709 --> 00:09:04,961
But this is…

207
00:09:06,462 --> 00:09:08,214
I feel like my knees might give out.

208
00:09:08,297 --> 00:09:10,883
- This is quite…
- Don't say that. We're the same age.

209
00:09:10,967 --> 00:09:12,885
Why would your knees give out?

210
00:09:12,969 --> 00:09:14,679
No, I can't. My legs are shaking.

211
00:09:16,347 --> 00:09:17,390
Nope.

212
00:09:17,473 --> 00:09:19,392
You have to straighten your knees.

213
00:09:21,519 --> 00:09:22,770
So this is how you do it.

214
00:09:23,938 --> 00:09:25,022
This is fun.

215
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:26,941
I'm drooling.

216
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:30,987
- Jun-ho, are we leaving at 9:30 a.m.?
- Yes.

217
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:32,363
- Are you going together?
- Yes.

218
00:09:32,446 --> 00:09:34,448
The three of us here.

219
00:09:34,532 --> 00:09:36,409
- And Smita and Snehal.
- And the twins?

220
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:39,912
ZUHA PUTS ON MAKE-UP WITH THE GUESTS

221
00:09:39,996 --> 00:09:41,414
You don't do shading?

222
00:09:41,497 --> 00:09:43,541
We're not good at make-up.

223
00:09:43,624 --> 00:09:45,835
- I contour and slim my face down.
- Me too.

224
00:09:45,918 --> 00:09:47,086
I'm doing that now.

225
00:09:47,169 --> 00:09:48,921
But your face is already slim enough.

226
00:09:51,882 --> 00:09:52,717
9:30 A.M.

227
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:54,385
We'll get going now.

228
00:09:54,468 --> 00:09:56,095
- Take care.
- We'll see you later.

229
00:09:56,178 --> 00:09:57,138
See you later.

230
00:09:57,221 --> 00:10:01,100
We should say goodbye
to those who are checking out then.

231
00:10:01,183 --> 00:10:02,351
Right, we should.

232
00:10:02,435 --> 00:10:04,478
Stay healthy and enjoy your school life.

233
00:10:04,562 --> 00:10:06,272
- Okay.
- Stay healthy. I'll see you again.

234
00:10:06,355 --> 00:10:08,649
- It was so fun thanks to you two.
- Likewise.

235
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:10,860
I'll never forget it.

236
00:10:10,943 --> 00:10:12,862
- Let's meet again sometime.
- Sure.

237
00:10:16,365 --> 00:10:18,117
- You grew close, right?
- Yes.

238
00:10:20,369 --> 00:10:21,495
Take care.

239
00:10:22,413 --> 00:10:24,123
- See you later.
- Have a safe trip.

240
00:10:24,206 --> 00:10:26,375
JUN-HO, SANG-CHEON,
SNEHAL, SMITA, AND SEUL GO OUT

241
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:28,044
Will you be ready by 10:50 a.m.?

242
00:10:28,127 --> 00:10:29,420
GETTING READY TO CHECK OUT

243
00:10:29,503 --> 00:10:31,505
How do I get my luggage out?

244
00:10:32,173 --> 00:10:33,591
I'll help you bring it down.

245
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:35,134
- Thank you.
- I got it.

246
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:37,011
- You can let go.
- it might spill out.

247
00:10:37,595 --> 00:10:39,013
Just stuff it in even if it's full.

248
00:10:39,096 --> 00:10:40,723
I'll take something out if it won't fit.

249
00:10:40,806 --> 00:10:42,850
Right, toss it if it doesn't fit.

250
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:43,976
NOISY

251
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:45,645
This is crazy.

252
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:52,777
THE BOSS GOES INTO THE SAUNA?

253
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:54,362
There's no privacy.

254
00:10:55,738 --> 00:10:57,281
Why am I so tired?

255
00:11:02,953 --> 00:11:03,871
What's this?

256
00:11:07,291 --> 00:11:09,085
- Did you sleep?
- Yeah.

257
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:13,297
I have no alone time.

258
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:16,842
How do you think karaoke was last night?

259
00:11:16,926 --> 00:11:17,760
It was fun.

260
00:11:17,843 --> 00:11:19,011
Was it okay?

261
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:20,221
Yeah, it was fun.

262
00:11:20,304 --> 00:11:21,972
You think they found it new and fun?

263
00:11:22,598 --> 00:11:23,432
Of course.

264
00:11:24,141 --> 00:11:25,976
Everything must've felt new to them.

265
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:28,687
- I talked to Seul and Jun-ho earlier
- Okay.

266
00:11:28,771 --> 00:11:30,940
And they wanted to try the jacuzzi.

267
00:11:31,023 --> 00:11:32,316
- Really?
- Yeah.

268
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:33,943
We should use it today then.

269
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:36,862
THE BOSS'S AMBITIOUS CREATION

270
00:11:37,446 --> 00:11:39,532
- We should use the jacuzzi a little.
- Yeah.

271
00:11:39,615 --> 00:11:40,866
DAY 3 EVENT
JACUZZI

272
00:11:41,492 --> 00:11:43,327
They're exchanging numbers.

273
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:46,497
- They're exchanging numbers now.
- Yeah?

274
00:11:47,456 --> 00:11:49,667
- They're leaving soon.
- Right.

275
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:51,210
Are they checking out at 11:00 a.m.?

276
00:11:51,293 --> 00:11:52,253
Yeah, out at 11:00 a.m.

277
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:54,797
Is there anything we can do for them?

278
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:58,050
Once they check out, it's all over.

279
00:11:58,134 --> 00:12:00,553
You know what makes you so kindhearted?

280
00:12:00,636 --> 00:12:01,762
No, what?

281
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:04,056
You keep wanting to do something for them.

282
00:12:04,849 --> 00:12:06,058
Is there anything we can do?

283
00:12:07,435 --> 00:12:10,146
I thought about new things to do
for guests checking out.

284
00:12:10,229 --> 00:12:11,981
I wanted to communicate with the guests,

285
00:12:12,064 --> 00:12:13,357
so that's what I thought about.

286
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:14,650
HOW WILL THEY DO IT?

287
00:12:15,401 --> 00:12:16,652
I'm feeling hungry.

288
00:12:20,197 --> 00:12:21,490
Are you eating lunch later?

289
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:22,741
Should I make something now?

290
00:12:22,825 --> 00:12:24,243
- Okay.
- Hey, you want to eat too?

291
00:12:24,326 --> 00:12:25,286
Sure.

292
00:12:25,369 --> 00:12:27,037
- I should do it now.
- What will you make?

293
00:12:27,746 --> 00:12:29,498
- I'll fry up last night's leftovers.
- Okay.

294
00:12:29,582 --> 00:12:31,542
BRUNCH
FRIED RICE WITH LEFTOVERS

295
00:12:32,209 --> 00:12:33,502
LEFTOVER NO. 1
COLD RICE

296
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:35,546
LEFTOVER NO. 2
CABBAGE SALAD

297
00:12:35,629 --> 00:12:36,881
I guess I can put all of it in.

298
00:12:38,549 --> 00:12:40,885
LEFTOVER NO. 3
PORK BELLY

299
00:12:47,183 --> 00:12:49,643
THE BOSS'S CABBAGE FRIED RICE

300
00:12:50,853 --> 00:12:52,146
It looks good.

301
00:12:52,229 --> 00:12:53,606
- Jun-ho.
- Yes?

302
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:55,649
Today's my birthday.

303
00:12:55,733 --> 00:12:57,401
- What would you like?
- What?

304
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:59,778
- What do you want for your birthday?
- Boss told me

305
00:12:59,862 --> 00:13:00,905
to get some rest.

306
00:13:00,988 --> 00:13:02,656
Then, rest. Don't even come up.

307
00:13:03,532 --> 00:13:05,409
- Rest.
- I can't. I'm climbing up.

308
00:13:07,661 --> 00:13:08,621
Gosh, I'm beat.

309
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:11,916
By the way, the way I see it,

310
00:13:11,999 --> 00:13:14,752
when new guests come,
we just say, "Hello!"

311
00:13:14,835 --> 00:13:17,254
- Right.
- And I think that's awkward.

312
00:13:17,338 --> 00:13:19,131
- There's no introduction.
- Right.

313
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:20,216
And we came out late.

314
00:13:20,299 --> 00:13:23,260
We should greet them
and introduce ourselves properly.

315
00:13:23,344 --> 00:13:25,596
So I bet they felt awkward yesterday.

316
00:13:26,388 --> 00:13:28,182
So, I thought we could serve
welcome drinks.

317
00:13:28,265 --> 00:13:30,518
- Welcome drinks?
- Yeah.

318
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:32,311
I thought of that too yesterday.

319
00:13:32,978 --> 00:13:34,396
YESTERDAY AFTERNOON

320
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,774
We should give them welcome drinks.

321
00:13:37,691 --> 00:13:41,153
When the guests came, they didn't know
what to do either, so it was a bit…

322
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:43,239
Maybe squeeze lemon juice into some water.

323
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:46,283
- It's like a juice detox.
- It's healthy. Yeah, it's good.

324
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:47,952
It's a healthy drink.

325
00:13:48,035 --> 00:13:49,537
Sounds good. Let's do that.

326
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:52,248
ZUHA COMES TO THE KITCHEN TOO

327
00:13:52,331 --> 00:13:53,499
- Hello.
- Hey.

328
00:13:53,582 --> 00:13:55,292
First, let's eat this.

329
00:13:55,376 --> 00:13:56,919
They'll leave at 11:00 a.m.

330
00:13:57,461 --> 00:13:58,963
- So, before they leave…
- Okay.

331
00:13:59,046 --> 00:14:01,715
Let's go to the table outside

332
00:14:01,799 --> 00:14:03,884
and ask them one by one

333
00:14:03,968 --> 00:14:06,220
how they liked their stay.

334
00:14:06,303 --> 00:14:07,638
You want to hear how they feel?

335
00:14:08,138 --> 00:14:10,432
- For the last time?
- As a sort of goodbye?

336
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:13,394
Yeah, I want to let them pick
who they want to talk to.

337
00:14:13,477 --> 00:14:15,062
GUESTS CHOOSE EMPLOYEES FOR THE CHAT

338
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:16,814
GUESTS WILL CHOOSE?

339
00:14:16,897 --> 00:14:18,399
- Oh, no.
- That's cruel.

340
00:14:18,482 --> 00:14:20,067
What if I don't get picked?

341
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:21,110
I'll cry.

342
00:14:21,193 --> 00:14:22,486
- You never know.
- You think so?

343
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:23,571
YOU NEVER KNOW

344
00:14:23,654 --> 00:14:25,155
Let's do that.

345
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:26,323
That's not bad.

346
00:14:26,991 --> 00:14:28,701
This should be ready, right?

347
00:14:28,784 --> 00:14:29,869
It's okay.

348
00:14:30,619 --> 00:14:31,662
Everyone, come on up.

349
00:14:31,745 --> 00:14:32,872
WITH GUESTS

350
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:33,789
Let's go.

351
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:35,291
We're serving you brunch. Hurry.

352
00:14:35,374 --> 00:14:36,834
BRUNCH BEFORE CHECKOUT

353
00:14:36,917 --> 00:14:38,878
- Thank you for the food.
- Thank you.

354
00:14:39,753 --> 00:14:40,921
Try it.

355
00:14:49,763 --> 00:14:51,432
- It's good.
- It's so good.

356
00:14:51,515 --> 00:14:52,516
Yeah.

357
00:14:53,934 --> 00:14:56,228
You want to stay longer, don't you?

358
00:14:56,312 --> 00:14:58,063
- Yes!
- Really?

359
00:14:58,147 --> 00:14:59,607
I hope you made some good memories.

360
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:01,191
I'll write them in my diary.

361
00:15:01,275 --> 00:15:02,484
Yeah, definitely.

362
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:04,987
My first memory as a 20-year-old.
It was great.

363
00:15:06,071 --> 00:15:07,990
Before you leave, for the last time…

364
00:15:08,073 --> 00:15:09,366
BEFORE WE LEAVE?

365
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:12,369
If you have an employee
you want to talk to,

366
00:15:13,245 --> 00:15:14,246
you can pick one

367
00:15:14,914 --> 00:15:15,998
to talk with before you go.

368
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:17,249
It's not a formal meeting.

369
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:18,918
- Just a casual talk.
- Yeah.

370
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:20,294
SURPRISED

371
00:15:20,377 --> 00:15:22,212
My heart is racing.

372
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:24,798
Boss thought it'd be nice
to do this before you leave.

373
00:15:24,882 --> 00:15:26,467
BOSS'S IDEA
TALKING TIME BEFORE CHECKOUT

374
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:29,720
And I'm not sure we'll have enough time.
It's our first try.

375
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:31,180
THEIR FIRST CHECKOUT SERVICE

376
00:15:31,263 --> 00:15:33,015
- Then, should we do it in pairs?
- Sure.

377
00:15:33,098 --> 00:15:34,308
- Do it in pairs.
- Sounds good.

378
00:15:34,391 --> 00:15:35,392
All right.

379
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:37,311
- Wait.
- No, wait. Hold on.

380
00:15:37,394 --> 00:15:39,772
- We can't give you much time.
- Wait. In that case…

381
00:15:39,855 --> 00:15:41,398
THEY HAVE A MEETING

382
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:42,650
What do we do?

383
00:15:42,733 --> 00:15:43,901
What do you mean?

384
00:15:43,984 --> 00:15:46,528
- I'm so torn.
- I like Yeon-koung.

385
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:49,907
And I'm sad because I didn't get to
talk much with Jun-ho.

386
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:51,700
And with Kian and Kazuha, I didn't get to…

387
00:15:51,784 --> 00:15:53,494
No, Hee-jeong. Then, that's everyone.

388
00:15:53,577 --> 00:15:54,828
We have to pick one.

389
00:15:54,912 --> 00:15:55,955
SHE CAN'T DECIDE

390
00:15:56,038 --> 00:15:57,957
Just pick one. It's nothing serious.

391
00:15:58,040 --> 00:15:59,124
Anyone you want.

392
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:00,668
I mean, we won't get hurt.

393
00:16:00,751 --> 00:16:02,836
We won't. It's all right.

394
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:03,796
Okay.

395
00:16:03,879 --> 00:16:05,214
HEE-JEONG AND JAE-EUN'S CHOICE

396
00:16:05,297 --> 00:16:06,632
Who will it be?

397
00:16:13,597 --> 00:16:14,431
- Me?
- Yes.

398
00:16:14,515 --> 00:16:16,725
Gosh, I was picked!

399
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:23,357
We were going to pick her. How could you?

400
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,818
BITTER

401
00:16:26,443 --> 00:16:29,405
- I've been so nice to you.
- But we were so torn.

402
00:16:29,488 --> 00:16:31,740
No, it's really all right.

403
00:16:31,824 --> 00:16:33,951
I guess it definitely wasn't Boss.

404
00:16:34,034 --> 00:16:35,661
No, that's not it!

405
00:16:35,744 --> 00:16:37,621
- Right?
- No! This is wrong. Wait.

406
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:39,540
This is a misunderstanding.

407
00:16:39,623 --> 00:16:40,541
All right.

408
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,501
Who do you want?

409
00:16:42,584 --> 00:16:44,712
IT'S TIME
FOR JEONG-WON AND DON-HEE TO PICK

410
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:46,171
- Don-hee. Yeah.
- Should we say it?

411
00:16:49,591 --> 00:16:51,176
GETTING HIS HOPES UP

412
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,136
All right.

413
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:55,305
- We pick you.
- Really?

414
00:16:55,389 --> 00:16:56,890
THEY PICK ZUHA

415
00:16:57,558 --> 00:16:59,018
We pick you.

416
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:04,481
I've been so nice to you guys.

417
00:17:05,107 --> 00:17:06,066
FLUSTERED

418
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:08,402
KNEELING

419
00:17:08,485 --> 00:17:10,487
And I'm the one who suggested this!

420
00:17:14,074 --> 00:17:15,701
- No, hold on!
- No!

421
00:17:15,784 --> 00:17:17,411
<i>I mean, we won't get hurt.</i>

422
00:17:17,494 --> 00:17:18,370
EMOTIONALLY DAMAGED

423
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:19,580
Go on ahead.

424
00:17:19,663 --> 00:17:20,706
We better do the dishes.

425
00:17:20,789 --> 00:17:22,833
We'll do the dishes in the meantime.

426
00:17:22,916 --> 00:17:24,001
Let's go.

427
00:17:28,756 --> 00:17:31,133
- What a special moment.
- I know.

428
00:17:34,136 --> 00:17:35,262
He came out.

429
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:38,557
KIAN FOLLOWS THEM OUT?

430
00:17:39,224 --> 00:17:40,559
I have to talk with him a bit.

431
00:17:41,310 --> 00:17:42,770
He has to throw out the food waste.

432
00:17:42,853 --> 00:17:43,687
HIM = FOOD WASTE

433
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:45,564
Don't worry about him.

434
00:17:45,647 --> 00:17:46,982
Yeah, go on.

435
00:17:47,816 --> 00:17:49,151
I need to have a talk with you.

436
00:17:49,234 --> 00:17:50,736
I'LL TALK TO THE FOOD WASTE

437
00:17:51,528 --> 00:17:53,280
How did you become food waste?

438
00:17:57,701 --> 00:17:59,912
AFTER A SHORT CONVERSATION, THEY PART WAYS

439
00:18:01,371 --> 00:18:04,291
I need to be really good to the guests.

440
00:18:04,917 --> 00:18:06,293
This kind of hurts.

441
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:08,295
STARING

442
00:18:08,378 --> 00:18:09,838
- Oh, no.
- Oh, no!

443
00:18:09,922 --> 00:18:12,174
BOSS

444
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:13,342
Darn it.

445
00:18:14,593 --> 00:18:15,761
HE STEPPED IN SOMETHING

446
00:18:16,762 --> 00:18:18,222
The weather's nice.

447
00:18:22,017 --> 00:18:23,519
Darn it, how do I open this?

448
00:18:26,146 --> 00:18:27,147
Hey, Jun-ho.

449
00:18:28,690 --> 00:18:29,900
- Jun-ho?
- Yes?

450
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:31,401
Sorry, but…

451
00:18:32,236 --> 00:18:33,070
Seriously?

452
00:18:33,153 --> 00:18:35,155
- Sorry.
- For real?

453
00:18:35,697 --> 00:18:36,907
It just happened.

454
00:18:36,990 --> 00:18:38,158
You want me to open the door?

455
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:39,576
I'm sorry, it's…

456
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:40,619
I'm cold.

457
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:43,997
Darn it! Put the kitchen
on the first floor next time!

458
00:18:49,294 --> 00:18:50,129
There you go.

459
00:18:50,629 --> 00:18:52,047
- Pull.
- One, two, three.

460
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:56,927
- Leave it like this.
- Okay.

461
00:18:59,263 --> 00:19:00,305
I have to go back up.

462
00:19:05,269 --> 00:19:07,855
It's tough to climb up now.

463
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:09,523
Good luck.

464
00:19:10,607 --> 00:19:12,693
- Let's go in.
- It looks so nice inside.

465
00:19:12,776 --> 00:19:15,112
BENCH NEXT TO SKATING RINK
OUTDOOR TENT

466
00:19:15,195 --> 00:19:18,490
So you start college in March, right?

467
00:19:18,574 --> 00:19:19,908
- As dance majors?
- Yes.

468
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:21,410
- Do your best with dance.
- Yes.

469
00:19:21,493 --> 00:19:22,703
- And study hard.
- Yes.

470
00:19:22,786 --> 00:19:23,996
And lose weight.

471
00:19:24,079 --> 00:19:25,122
Why keep saying that?

472
00:19:25,205 --> 00:19:26,915
DANCE MAJORS ALWAYS WATCH THEIR WEIGHT

473
00:19:26,999 --> 00:19:29,334
Most people lose weight
like cramming for entrance exams.

474
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:31,044
- Right.
- Everyone does that.

475
00:19:31,128 --> 00:19:34,882
It's like studying. You cram
and forget everything after the test.

476
00:19:34,965 --> 00:19:36,049
ARTS AND SPORTS CAN RELATE

477
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:37,467
It's the same thing.

478
00:19:37,551 --> 00:19:39,136
- But you always…
- Yeah?

479
00:19:39,219 --> 00:19:41,513
It seems like you always
keep that balance.

480
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:44,558
Have you ever wanted to give up?
Like, "I can't do this anymore."

481
00:19:44,641 --> 00:19:45,475
Many times.

482
00:19:45,559 --> 00:19:47,102
You have a breakdown at times, right?

483
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:48,520
YEON-KOUNG'S WAY TO PERSEVERE

484
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:50,105
There are many different ways,

485
00:19:50,189 --> 00:19:53,358
but whenever you feel like that,
you'll have people who support you.

486
00:19:53,442 --> 00:19:54,276
Right.

487
00:19:55,068 --> 00:19:58,280
They believed in me
and that I could succeed,

488
00:19:58,363 --> 00:20:00,699
so I didn't want to let them down.

489
00:20:00,782 --> 00:20:03,911
And even when I wanted to quit,
I had that sense of responsibility.

490
00:20:03,994 --> 00:20:06,914
And it made me pull myself together
and keep going.

491
00:20:07,581 --> 00:20:12,169
So I hope you two
will control things like that.

492
00:20:12,252 --> 00:20:13,337
You're in your twenties.

493
00:20:14,171 --> 00:20:16,131
So, you can build your future slowly.

494
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:19,426
I think this will stay deep
in my heart for a long time.

495
00:20:19,509 --> 00:20:22,095
- I'll always remember this.
- Right, exactly.

496
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:23,222
That's good to hear.

497
00:20:24,723 --> 00:20:26,683
Is there something you want to do?

498
00:20:26,767 --> 00:20:28,227
- In the future?
- Yeah.

499
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:31,438
As for me, I want to become
the best in my field.

500
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:33,732
- I want to…
- You should dream big.

501
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:36,693
Yes, I want to become
the top expert in the field.

502
00:20:37,444 --> 00:20:39,321
- And I want to become famous.
- Famous?

503
00:20:39,404 --> 00:20:41,281
Yes, my dream is
to become famous in my field.

504
00:20:41,907 --> 00:20:42,783
That's cool.

505
00:20:42,866 --> 00:20:43,700
Please root for me.

506
00:20:43,784 --> 00:20:45,452
Of course, I will.

507
00:20:45,535 --> 00:20:48,372
If you have a goal

508
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:52,960
and imagine yourself achieving it,

509
00:20:53,043 --> 00:20:54,962
isn't it quite exciting?

510
00:20:55,045 --> 00:20:57,673
- Myself being successful?
- Yes, imagining it.

511
00:20:57,756 --> 00:20:58,590
You can do it.

512
00:20:58,674 --> 00:21:00,133
- Yes, I can do it.
- Yes, thank you.

513
00:21:01,677 --> 00:21:03,887
- We had just gotten close.
- Right, so it feels sadder.

514
00:21:03,971 --> 00:21:05,389
It's sad that you're leaving.

515
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:09,101
- We won't forget this.
- This was a great start to our twenties.

516
00:21:09,726 --> 00:21:10,602
Boss, we're back.

517
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:12,312
- Was it a good talk?
- Yeah.

518
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:13,397
Did you have a good time?

519
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:15,315
What did they say?

520
00:21:15,399 --> 00:21:17,693
When they were with us,
they were pretty different

521
00:21:17,776 --> 00:21:19,444
from when they were with the others.

522
00:21:19,528 --> 00:21:21,738
- I bet.
- Yeah, their energy was different.

523
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:23,448
SOMEWHAT JEALOUS

524
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:25,826
I enjoyed my time too.

525
00:21:25,909 --> 00:21:27,202
It was therapeutic.

526
00:21:29,746 --> 00:21:31,248
It's time to check out now.

527
00:21:31,331 --> 00:21:33,292
You can write
in the visitors' log if you want.

528
00:21:34,001 --> 00:21:35,836
- Let's write something.
- Okay.

529
00:21:35,919 --> 00:21:37,212
WRITING IN THE VISITORS' LOG

530
00:21:37,838 --> 00:21:40,424
<i>Kian's B&B will be remembered forever.</i>

531
00:21:42,634 --> 00:21:44,678
<i>I'll make it big and come back.</i>

532
00:21:45,637 --> 00:21:47,097
<i>Should I write, "Let's go, 07s"?</i>

533
00:21:48,348 --> 00:21:49,558
<i>All done.</i>

534
00:21:49,641 --> 00:21:51,476
- MAY THIS BE REMEMBERED FOREVER
- HEE-JEONG

535
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:53,395
- KIAN'S B&B'S POWER BILL IS ON ME
- JEONG-WON

536
00:21:54,855 --> 00:21:57,024
SOUND OF WRITING ON PAPER

537
00:21:57,107 --> 00:21:59,318
YEON-KOUNG'S PREPARING SOMETHING

538
00:22:00,110 --> 00:22:01,361
TO JAE-EUN

539
00:22:02,237 --> 00:22:04,448
They're nothing special. I have my books…

540
00:22:04,531 --> 00:22:05,490
This is awesome.

541
00:22:05,574 --> 00:22:06,908
AUTOGRAPHED BOOKS

542
00:22:06,992 --> 00:22:07,909
I have stuff too.

543
00:22:09,870 --> 00:22:10,871
Thank you.

544
00:22:10,954 --> 00:22:12,873
ZUHA'S ALBUM

545
00:22:12,956 --> 00:22:14,249
Mine are pajamas.

546
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:15,584
- One for everyone.
- Thank you.

547
00:22:15,667 --> 00:22:17,085
Weren't you wearing this?

548
00:22:17,169 --> 00:22:18,920
- Yes, they're the same.
- Thank you.

549
00:22:20,255 --> 00:22:22,466
I should give them something too.

550
00:22:25,844 --> 00:22:27,095
Goodness.

551
00:22:27,721 --> 00:22:28,847
I don't have anything.

552
00:22:40,776 --> 00:22:42,736
All right, kids. Have one of these.

553
00:22:43,904 --> 00:22:44,905
Thank you.

554
00:22:45,864 --> 00:22:46,823
Hold on.

555
00:22:46,907 --> 00:22:48,575
Vegetable juice.

556
00:22:50,035 --> 00:22:50,952
Thank you.

557
00:22:54,289 --> 00:22:55,290
I won't drink this.

558
00:22:55,373 --> 00:22:57,876
- I was so thirsty, but I won't drink it.
- Seriously.

559
00:22:57,959 --> 00:23:00,420
She said, "I was so thirsty"!

560
00:23:00,504 --> 00:23:01,630
Vegetable juice.

561
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:04,132
- We'll get going now.
- Thanks for coming.

562
00:23:04,216 --> 00:23:05,759
Okay. I'll be rooting for you.

563
00:23:05,842 --> 00:23:07,177
- Hey, all the best.
- Thank you.

564
00:23:07,260 --> 00:23:08,261
Take care of yourselves.

565
00:23:08,845 --> 00:23:09,805
Bye.

566
00:23:09,888 --> 00:23:11,807
- Bye.
- Thank you.

567
00:23:11,890 --> 00:23:13,892
SAD

568
00:23:13,975 --> 00:23:16,019
- Thank you.
- Take care!

569
00:23:16,812 --> 00:23:18,772
- We wish you the best!
- Bye!

570
00:23:20,107 --> 00:23:21,525
It's hard to leave.

571
00:23:21,608 --> 00:23:23,610
- Why did it feel so short?
- Right?

572
00:23:23,693 --> 00:23:24,986
Let's save it in our hearts.

573
00:23:25,070 --> 00:23:27,989
Right. Let's take a last look and go.

574
00:23:28,073 --> 00:23:32,035
<i>It was like a house I dreamed of</i>
<i>when I was a kid.</i>

575
00:23:32,119 --> 00:23:34,996
<i>We had drinks</i>

576
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:36,957
<i>and talked together.</i>

577
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:38,875
<i>I thought, "This is what being young is."</i>

578
00:23:38,959 --> 00:23:40,210
KIAN'S B&B IS ABOUT "YOUTH"

579
00:23:40,293 --> 00:23:44,172
<i>The surroundings, the house,</i>
<i>and the people were all so romantic.</i>

580
00:23:44,256 --> 00:23:45,590
<i>That was a dream to me.</i>

581
00:23:45,674 --> 00:23:46,675
KIAN'S B&B IS "ROMANTIC"

582
00:23:46,758 --> 00:23:48,135
<i>Five stars.</i>

583
00:23:48,218 --> 00:23:50,220
<i>Because imagination became reality there.</i>

584
00:23:50,303 --> 00:23:51,513
It's been fun.

585
00:23:51,596 --> 00:23:53,682
- I hope you hit it big, Kian's B&B.
- I hope so too.

586
00:23:53,765 --> 00:23:55,016
THE FOUR OF THEM CHECK OUT

587
00:23:56,101 --> 00:23:58,562
Our first guests have left.

588
00:23:59,187 --> 00:24:01,273
The empty beds feel so strange.

589
00:24:03,191 --> 00:24:05,485
We have to clean those empty spaces too.

590
00:24:05,569 --> 00:24:07,195
Clean the second and third floors?

591
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:08,655
We should dust the blankets off.

592
00:24:08,738 --> 00:24:10,240
Jun-ho, let's dust this off.

593
00:24:10,323 --> 00:24:11,408
Okay.

594
00:24:14,161 --> 00:24:16,496
HUGE T-SHIRT COMFORTER

595
00:24:16,580 --> 00:24:17,414
- Let's go.
- Go.

596
00:24:17,497 --> 00:24:18,957
SHOUTS

597
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:22,002
Hold tighter. The edge.

598
00:24:26,673 --> 00:24:28,216
We should do it ten times.

599
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:29,217
We've done five.

600
00:24:29,301 --> 00:24:30,802
- Go. Six.
- One.

601
00:24:30,886 --> 00:24:31,761
Two.

602
00:24:32,387 --> 00:24:33,305
- Three.
- Three.

603
00:24:33,847 --> 00:24:35,807
Okay. Fold it like this.

604
00:24:39,186 --> 00:24:40,604
- Are you good?
- Yes.

605
00:24:43,440 --> 00:24:45,025
- She's good at climbing that.
- Right?

606
00:24:46,401 --> 00:24:49,196
CLEANING THOROUGHLY

607
00:25:02,959 --> 00:25:04,628
BOSS FOUND SOMETHING

608
00:25:05,587 --> 00:25:07,005
Plastic bags…

609
00:25:07,088 --> 00:25:08,381
Gosh, my arms.

610
00:25:09,633 --> 00:25:10,717
Here they are.

611
00:25:10,800 --> 00:25:12,510
BRINGING A PLASTIC BAG

612
00:25:15,889 --> 00:25:17,515
Kian, we threw out the food waste.

613
00:25:17,599 --> 00:25:19,768
And we can throw out
recyclables tomorrow, right?

614
00:25:19,851 --> 00:25:21,853
Hey, there's something…

615
00:25:22,604 --> 00:25:23,605
The toilet.

616
00:25:23,688 --> 00:25:25,106
- The toilet? What's wrong?
- I mean…

617
00:25:25,857 --> 00:25:26,858
The toilet bowl?

618
00:25:26,942 --> 00:25:29,069
No. Let's empty the bathroom bin together.

619
00:25:29,152 --> 00:25:30,612
- Sure.
- And we should…

620
00:25:31,238 --> 00:25:32,739
put it in this.

621
00:25:32,822 --> 00:25:34,241
Why? Is there a lot?

622
00:25:34,908 --> 00:25:35,909
Well, I think…

623
00:25:35,992 --> 00:25:36,826
AT A LOSS

624
00:25:36,910 --> 00:25:38,036
Is something scary in there?

625
00:25:38,787 --> 00:25:40,413
NERVOUS

626
00:25:40,497 --> 00:25:41,414
Well, it is possible.

627
00:25:41,498 --> 00:25:42,332
BEING VAGUE

628
00:25:42,916 --> 00:25:43,875
Got it.

629
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:45,794
So let's throw this out first.

630
00:25:45,877 --> 00:25:47,921
- Let's empty it in here.
- In there? Combine them?

631
00:25:50,799 --> 00:25:53,468
Now, if we put them together…

632
00:25:54,928 --> 00:25:56,137
It's not a lot, but…

633
00:25:57,430 --> 00:25:58,473
Please.

634
00:25:59,683 --> 00:26:01,268
- There won't be anything.
- That won't…

635
00:26:18,451 --> 00:26:20,453
- Lift it.
- Here. Put it in.

636
00:26:20,537 --> 00:26:22,205
Put it in.

637
00:26:22,289 --> 00:26:23,873
Just put it in here.

638
00:26:29,879 --> 00:26:30,797
Wait. Then…

639
00:26:31,423 --> 00:26:32,507
I'll use this to…

640
00:26:34,718 --> 00:26:36,344
- Lift it.
- I…

641
00:26:37,762 --> 00:26:39,306
I've never seen…

642
00:26:40,098 --> 00:26:42,559
- other people's poop before in my life.
- Really?

643
00:26:42,642 --> 00:26:43,977
Hello.

644
00:26:44,060 --> 00:26:45,562
IN 38 YEARS OF MY LIFE

645
00:26:45,645 --> 00:26:47,230
19 YEARS SINCE MY DEBUT

646
00:26:49,524 --> 00:26:52,444
- I've never seen other people's poop.
- Really?

647
00:26:52,527 --> 00:26:53,611
Never?

648
00:26:54,404 --> 00:26:56,656
- I mean…
- In Season 1, I saw some.

649
00:26:56,740 --> 00:26:58,575
But it's weird to see it again.

650
00:27:05,290 --> 00:27:06,374
PRESSING DOWN

651
00:27:06,458 --> 00:27:08,543
It's been a while, so it's shocking.

652
00:27:08,626 --> 00:27:10,795
THE SHOCKING THING
HE HASN'T SEEN IN A WHILE

653
00:27:11,838 --> 00:27:13,089
Hey, this is…

654
00:27:13,173 --> 00:27:15,300
- We should've put a bag in.
- My goodness.

655
00:27:15,383 --> 00:27:16,760
- To throw it out like that?
- Yeah.

656
00:27:16,843 --> 00:27:18,845
- Okay, throw it out now.
- I'll go throw it out.

657
00:27:21,931 --> 00:27:23,683
HE THROWS IT OUT

658
00:27:23,767 --> 00:27:25,852
Gosh, that was so funny.

659
00:27:25,935 --> 00:27:28,480
HE PUTS THE BIN BACK
WITH A GARBAGE BAG INSIDE

660
00:27:28,563 --> 00:27:31,733
SCRUBBING HARD

661
00:27:31,816 --> 00:27:33,068
- Zuha.
- Yes?

662
00:27:33,151 --> 00:27:36,196
Do you think
we should empty the bin or not?

663
00:27:36,279 --> 00:27:38,615
It's not too full yet.

664
00:27:38,698 --> 00:27:39,616
- Right?
- Yes.

665
00:27:39,699 --> 00:27:42,035
It's best to put
a plastic bag in the bin first.

666
00:27:42,660 --> 00:27:44,245
- Know what I mean?
- You're right.

667
00:27:44,329 --> 00:27:45,622
- We just emptied ours.
- Hold on.

668
00:27:45,705 --> 00:27:46,623
ADVICE FROM EXPERIENCE

669
00:27:50,543 --> 00:27:51,961
We'll do it tomorrow.

670
00:27:52,045 --> 00:27:53,421
Did we clean everything?

671
00:27:54,005 --> 00:27:55,298
- I think we're all done.
- Right?

672
00:27:55,382 --> 00:27:56,758
LET'S GET SOME REST

673
00:27:56,841 --> 00:27:58,343
Why am I hungry?

674
00:27:58,426 --> 00:28:00,095
What's for lunch today, Boss?

675
00:28:00,595 --> 00:28:02,222
- Seaweed soup for you.
- Seaweed soup?

676
00:28:02,305 --> 00:28:04,516
Shouldn't we have it
since it's your birthday?

677
00:28:04,599 --> 00:28:06,267
Then, we should go buy some seaweed.

678
00:28:06,351 --> 00:28:08,019
- I bought it.
- What?

679
00:28:08,103 --> 00:28:09,145
I bought it yesterday.

680
00:28:09,854 --> 00:28:11,523
You bought that?

681
00:28:13,608 --> 00:28:15,610
WELL-HIDDEN SEAWEED

682
00:28:16,277 --> 00:28:19,614
We hid it there
so that you wouldn't find out.

683
00:28:19,697 --> 00:28:20,698
Really?

684
00:28:20,782 --> 00:28:22,534
You really didn't catch on yesterday?

685
00:28:22,617 --> 00:28:23,493
I didn't.

686
00:28:24,202 --> 00:28:25,453
It was perfect.

687
00:28:25,537 --> 00:28:27,205
Anyways, I feel embarrassed.

688
00:28:27,288 --> 00:28:28,748
So you'll make seaweed soup for me?

689
00:28:28,832 --> 00:28:30,125
- We will, but…
- Yeah?

690
00:28:30,208 --> 00:28:33,169
I've never made it for ten people,
so I don't know how much to make.

691
00:28:33,253 --> 00:28:34,546
You're going to make it?

692
00:28:34,629 --> 00:28:36,172
- Yes.
- That's good.

693
00:28:36,673 --> 00:28:37,799
Actually, Jun-ho,

694
00:28:37,882 --> 00:28:40,176
why don't you be the main chef today?

695
00:28:40,260 --> 00:28:41,970
- Seriously?
- How about that?

696
00:28:42,053 --> 00:28:43,680
BOSS'S IDEA
TAKE TURNS BEING MAIN CHEF

697
00:28:43,763 --> 00:28:47,350
That way, the guests can know
who's cooking and feel excited.

698
00:28:47,434 --> 00:28:49,018
I'll do it tomorrow.

699
00:28:49,644 --> 00:28:50,812
What do you say?

700
00:28:50,895 --> 00:28:52,313
Why am I going first?

701
00:28:52,397 --> 00:28:54,107
He must be feeling pressured.

702
00:28:54,607 --> 00:28:56,818
Then, I think I should start cooking now.

703
00:28:58,778 --> 00:29:00,238
It's going to take that long?

704
00:29:00,321 --> 00:29:01,740
You're that unsure of yourself?

705
00:29:01,823 --> 00:29:03,408
I need to think about the recipes.

706
00:29:03,491 --> 00:29:05,326
You're going to cook for six hours?

707
00:29:05,410 --> 00:29:06,828
Will I get a proper dinner?

708
00:29:06,911 --> 00:29:08,413
Or should I have some snacks?

709
00:29:08,496 --> 00:29:09,456
We have many snacks.

710
00:29:12,417 --> 00:29:13,752
We should go to the supermarket.

711
00:29:13,835 --> 00:29:16,546
Right, let's go grocery shopping.

712
00:29:16,629 --> 00:29:18,965
- Dharma Teacher, I'm in your hands.
- Sure.

713
00:29:19,048 --> 00:29:20,300
Let's talk casually.

714
00:29:20,383 --> 00:29:22,010
THEY WERE ALL BORN IN 1998

715
00:29:26,347 --> 00:29:28,933
DAEGWALLYEONG SAFARI FARM

716
00:29:29,017 --> 00:29:30,310
<i>It's so picturesque.</i>

717
00:29:32,479 --> 00:29:34,272
<i>That horse is beautiful.</i>

718
00:29:34,355 --> 00:29:35,523
<i>It's so beautiful.</i>

719
00:29:36,900 --> 00:29:40,028
THEY'RE HERE FOR HORSEBACK RIDING

720
00:29:40,111 --> 00:29:42,781
FIRST TIME FOR THE FOUR BEGINNERS

721
00:29:42,864 --> 00:29:45,116
I've ridden horses
in the country for ten years.

722
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:47,994
But I'll take it easy and ride it safely.

723
00:29:48,578 --> 00:29:49,788
THE EXPERIENCED ONE GOES FIRST

724
00:29:49,871 --> 00:29:50,914
Then, I'll try it first.

725
00:29:55,502 --> 00:29:57,170
I guess you've wanted to run too.

726
00:29:59,923 --> 00:30:02,133
It looks like a scene from a movie.

727
00:30:02,217 --> 00:30:04,010
- He looks cool.
- He does.

728
00:30:04,636 --> 00:30:06,930
THE BEGINNERS TRY IT TOO

729
00:30:07,555 --> 00:30:09,140
The scenery is so nice.

730
00:30:10,183 --> 00:30:11,476
I like this.

731
00:30:13,144 --> 00:30:15,146
It's so cute to have
the dog come up with us.

732
00:30:16,898 --> 00:30:19,234
I didn't know horses were so charming.

733
00:30:19,317 --> 00:30:20,193
They're beautiful.

734
00:30:20,276 --> 00:30:21,486
Hooray!

735
00:30:26,533 --> 00:30:27,909
- This was fun.
- This was fun.

736
00:30:27,992 --> 00:30:29,202
It was so much fun.

737
00:30:29,285 --> 00:30:31,371
- Have a good time!
- We'll see you later.

738
00:30:31,454 --> 00:30:32,872
AFTER HORSEBACK RIDING

739
00:30:32,956 --> 00:30:34,082
SKY RANCH
POTTERY CAFE

740
00:30:34,165 --> 00:30:35,792
<i>It's huge.</i>

741
00:30:35,875 --> 00:30:38,336
<i>- The closer we get, the bigger it gets.</i>
<i>- It looks bigger.</i>

742
00:30:39,420 --> 00:30:42,173
NAKSANSA TEMPLE, YANGYANG

743
00:30:42,799 --> 00:30:44,342
NAKSANSA TEMPLE, YANGYANG

744
00:30:44,425 --> 00:30:46,261
Naksansa's so big.

745
00:30:46,344 --> 00:30:47,720
It's huge and beautiful.

746
00:30:47,804 --> 00:30:49,848
A BEAUTIFUL TEMPLE
OVERLOOKING THE EAST SEA

747
00:30:49,931 --> 00:30:52,892
Let me know if you have a question.
I'll be your guide.

748
00:30:52,976 --> 00:30:53,893
I appreciate it.

749
00:30:53,977 --> 00:30:58,064
If you take a look,
most temples by the sea

750
00:30:58,147 --> 00:31:00,275
have statues of Guanyin
overlooking the sea.

751
00:31:00,358 --> 00:31:01,860
- Guanyin overlooking the sea?
- Yes.

752
00:31:01,943 --> 00:31:04,112
I'll just follow you around today.

753
00:31:05,029 --> 00:31:05,989
I learned a new thing.

754
00:31:06,072 --> 00:31:08,992
Temples by the sea
have Guanyin statues overlooking the sea.

755
00:31:09,075 --> 00:31:11,119
GUANYIN OVERLOOKING THE SEA

756
00:31:15,498 --> 00:31:16,958
Do you want to ring the bell?

757
00:31:17,041 --> 00:31:19,586
I do it often at my temple.

758
00:31:19,669 --> 00:31:20,545
But you…

759
00:31:21,546 --> 00:31:24,799
THE PRIEST TRIES IT

760
00:31:24,883 --> 00:31:26,342
Do you want to do <i>giwabulsa?</i>

761
00:31:26,426 --> 00:31:27,719
What is that?

762
00:31:28,344 --> 00:31:30,972
A RITUAL WHERE YOU WRITE
YOUR WISHES ON CLAY ROOF TILES

763
00:31:31,055 --> 00:31:32,640
MAY MY WISHES COME TRUE

764
00:31:32,724 --> 00:31:36,728
It means, "Seek enlightenment above
and save others below."

765
00:31:36,811 --> 00:31:39,272
<i>- "Sangubori Hahwajungsaeng"?</i>
- Yes.

766
00:31:39,355 --> 00:31:42,901
I'll write, "Love, mercy, and peace."

767
00:31:43,526 --> 00:31:45,695
CAPTURING THE MOMENT
WHEN RELIGIONS UNITED

768
00:31:45,778 --> 00:31:46,946
Thank you.

769
00:31:47,030 --> 00:31:48,197
<i>Thanks to you,</i>

770
00:31:48,781 --> 00:31:50,950
<i>I'll never forget my time</i>
<i>at Naksansa Temple.</i>

771
00:31:51,034 --> 00:31:52,827
Now, let's buy what we need.

772
00:31:52,911 --> 00:31:54,162
THE STAFF ARRIVES AT THE MARKET

773
00:31:54,245 --> 00:31:55,788
We're doing welcome drinks, right?

774
00:31:55,872 --> 00:31:57,874
Here. Lemon juice. Get the good ones.

775
00:31:57,957 --> 00:31:58,958
- This one?
- Yeah.

776
00:32:01,836 --> 00:32:03,046
Should we go back now?

777
00:32:03,129 --> 00:32:04,756
Let's have some outside food this time.

778
00:32:04,839 --> 00:32:06,507
- Here is your bread.
- Thank you.

779
00:32:06,591 --> 00:32:08,384
It does look delicious.

780
00:32:08,468 --> 00:32:09,928
HERE FOR DAEGWALLYEONG POTATO BREAD

781
00:32:19,312 --> 00:32:20,855
BOSS USES HIS HANDS

782
00:32:28,738 --> 00:32:30,949
The coffee makes me feel much better.

783
00:32:31,032 --> 00:32:32,909
- I feel energetic now.
- Right.

784
00:32:32,992 --> 00:32:34,744
Boss looks a bit listless.

785
00:32:34,827 --> 00:32:36,579
- Do I?
- Yeah, don't you think so?

786
00:32:37,455 --> 00:32:38,414
I'll try to dig deep.

787
00:32:38,498 --> 00:32:40,124
Doesn't he look tired?

788
00:32:40,208 --> 00:32:41,250
I am.

789
00:32:41,876 --> 00:32:43,461
Why don't we do this today?

790
00:32:44,003 --> 00:32:46,005
When we have dinner,

791
00:32:46,089 --> 00:32:48,466
- we always sit in a circle.
- Right.

792
00:32:48,549 --> 00:32:50,343
I don't really like that.

793
00:32:50,426 --> 00:32:52,261
- Then what?
- I want us to be freer.

794
00:32:52,345 --> 00:32:53,721
Do you have an alternative?

795
00:32:53,805 --> 00:32:55,431
Like a hotel breakfast,

796
00:32:55,515 --> 00:32:59,268
what if people get their food
and eat wherever they want?

797
00:32:59,352 --> 00:33:00,812
How about that?

798
00:33:00,895 --> 00:33:02,146
Right now, it feels too…

799
00:33:02,230 --> 00:33:04,399
- Eat wherever they want?
- Yeah.

800
00:33:04,482 --> 00:33:06,901
Right now, being in one big group
is too much.

801
00:33:09,362 --> 00:33:11,239
That's my opinion. What do you think?

802
00:33:11,322 --> 00:33:12,824
But I like the way it is.

803
00:33:12,907 --> 00:33:14,242
- You like that?
- Yeah.

804
00:33:14,325 --> 00:33:17,120
There are old guests and new ones.

805
00:33:17,203 --> 00:33:20,707
Dinner's the only time
when they can all spend time together.

806
00:33:21,958 --> 00:33:24,836
And that's when they can
get to know each other.

807
00:33:24,919 --> 00:33:27,672
"Hello, today's my first day.
My name is so-and-so."

808
00:33:27,755 --> 00:33:29,173
"Is that so? Nice to meet you."

809
00:33:29,257 --> 00:33:31,300
- It's like that.
- Really?

810
00:33:31,384 --> 00:33:32,760
What do you think, Zuha?

811
00:33:32,844 --> 00:33:37,473
Me? Well, that's our first chance
to talk to new guests, so I liked it too.

812
00:33:37,557 --> 00:33:39,183
- You liked it?
- You did? See?

813
00:33:39,267 --> 00:33:40,435
Last night's karaoke too.

814
00:33:40,518 --> 00:33:43,980
They talked and danced
in separate small groups.

815
00:33:44,063 --> 00:33:47,358
The karaoke room.
I feel the same about that too.

816
00:33:47,442 --> 00:33:48,317
What about it?

817
00:33:48,401 --> 00:33:51,070
With the karaoke room,
it goes, "Okay, we're about to begin."

818
00:33:51,154 --> 00:33:52,447
- And everyone looks.
- Right.

819
00:33:52,530 --> 00:33:54,157
That's like a forced group activity too.

820
00:33:54,240 --> 00:33:57,535
It's because there actually aren't
many things we all do together.

821
00:33:57,618 --> 00:33:58,828
- So…
- There aren't?

822
00:33:58,911 --> 00:33:59,954
No.

823
00:34:00,038 --> 00:34:01,456
From the guests' perspective.

824
00:34:01,539 --> 00:34:04,083
- Really?
- What do we do together besides dinner?

825
00:34:04,167 --> 00:34:06,461
When we have drinks,
people break off into groups.

826
00:34:06,544 --> 00:34:08,755
EMPLOYEES SUPPORTING GROUP
VS BOSS SUPPORTING FREEDOM

827
00:34:09,338 --> 00:34:11,174
And those who want to drink join them.

828
00:34:11,257 --> 00:34:12,341
Come to think of it…

829
00:34:13,676 --> 00:34:15,678
Then, let's not change things.

830
00:34:15,762 --> 00:34:17,972
Let's just eat in a circle today then.

831
00:34:18,056 --> 00:34:18,931
All right.

832
00:34:19,432 --> 00:34:20,683
And about the door.

833
00:34:21,684 --> 00:34:23,561
I keep wanting to compromise.

834
00:34:24,353 --> 00:34:27,231
When you went outside
to talk with them earlier,

835
00:34:27,315 --> 00:34:28,399
he was doing the dishes.

836
00:34:28,483 --> 00:34:29,484
Okay.

837
00:34:29,567 --> 00:34:30,693
I couldn't open the door.

838
00:34:31,444 --> 00:34:33,237
It's too tough.

839
00:34:33,321 --> 00:34:34,947
BOSS WANTS COMPROMISE ON DOOR

840
00:34:35,031 --> 00:34:36,491
But we can't keep it open.

841
00:34:36,574 --> 00:34:37,408
COMPROMISE REJECTED

842
00:34:37,492 --> 00:34:39,952
But we, as the staff,
come and go so often.

843
00:34:40,036 --> 00:34:40,953
Still, it's a rule.

844
00:34:41,037 --> 00:34:41,871
REJECTED AGAIN

845
00:34:43,372 --> 00:34:45,958
I mean, let's make an exception
for the staff.

846
00:34:46,042 --> 00:34:47,710
- I'll open it for you.
- What?

847
00:34:47,794 --> 00:34:50,088
No, it's not like
you're there all the time.

848
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:52,256
Kazuha will open it for you.

849
00:34:53,299 --> 00:34:54,926
All right. Let's do that.

850
00:34:57,804 --> 00:35:00,389
- We can't lose hope and dreams.
- Right.

851
00:35:00,473 --> 00:35:02,308
Guys, don't forget. Hope and dreams.

852
00:35:02,391 --> 00:35:03,601
I shouldn't think this way.

853
00:35:06,938 --> 00:35:08,189
You're getting a call.

854
00:35:09,482 --> 00:35:10,608
Is it a guest calling?

855
00:35:12,068 --> 00:35:13,486
- Hello?
<i>- Hello?</i>

856
00:35:13,569 --> 00:35:14,529
Hello.

857
00:35:14,612 --> 00:35:17,990
We're heading
to Kian's B&B now to check in.

858
00:35:18,074 --> 00:35:19,659
How many of you are there?

859
00:35:19,742 --> 00:35:20,868
Three people.

860
00:35:21,911 --> 00:35:22,995
I see. Three?

861
00:35:23,079 --> 00:35:24,288
Where are you?

862
00:35:24,372 --> 00:35:25,915
We're in Pyeongchang right now.

863
00:35:25,998 --> 00:35:30,086
Then, I'll send you the address.

864
00:35:30,169 --> 00:35:33,089
<i>Okay. Then, we'll go there right now.</i>

865
00:35:33,881 --> 00:35:34,715
WE'RE STILL OUT

866
00:35:34,799 --> 00:35:37,009
No, you can't come in if you arrive now.

867
00:35:37,093 --> 00:35:38,427
<i>Can't we wait in the car?</i>

868
00:35:38,511 --> 00:35:41,264
Wait, so you have nowhere to go right now?

869
00:35:41,931 --> 00:35:43,432
<i>- No.</i>
- Then, you should come now.

870
00:35:43,516 --> 00:35:44,809
<i>Okay. Thank you.</i>

871
00:35:45,768 --> 00:35:46,894
Okay, let's go now.

872
00:35:46,978 --> 00:35:48,104
Let's get this packed to go.

873
00:35:48,187 --> 00:35:49,272
RETURNING EARLY AGAIN TODAY

874
00:35:49,355 --> 00:35:50,356
KIAN'S B&B ENTRANCE

875
00:35:50,439 --> 00:35:51,774
It's deep in the mountains.

876
00:35:51,858 --> 00:35:53,568
It's like going to a military camp.

877
00:35:55,236 --> 00:35:56,946
- What is it?
- I think that's it.

878
00:35:57,029 --> 00:35:59,073
The orange roof.

879
00:35:59,157 --> 00:36:00,575
Yeah! It says "Kian's B&B."

880
00:36:00,658 --> 00:36:01,701
ORANGE ROOF SPOTTED

881
00:36:01,784 --> 00:36:02,785
It's huge.

882
00:36:02,869 --> 00:36:05,413
It's like a big version
of a dog house in the countryside.

883
00:36:05,496 --> 00:36:06,873
Let's unload our luggage.

884
00:36:06,956 --> 00:36:08,124
Let's do that.

885
00:36:08,207 --> 00:36:09,125
Who could that be?

886
00:36:09,625 --> 00:36:10,626
I can't see inside.

887
00:36:10,710 --> 00:36:12,003
THE STAFF ARRIVE TOO

888
00:36:12,086 --> 00:36:13,129
Hello.

889
00:36:14,505 --> 00:36:16,090
